{
  "requirement": "The outline uses the file snapshot retained by the domain’s cache. Each item includes its kind and a reference the agent can pass to `read_node`. Follow `next` to see more items.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.outline_source.behavior`. I did not run them.\n\nThe requirement has four obligations. I mapped each to a test:\n\n1. **Snapshot retained by the domain's cache.**\n   - `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items]` writes `code.rs` and outlines it. It then overwrites the file with `fn changed() {}` and outlines again. It asserts the second `items` equal the first, so a re-read of the changed file would fail.\n   - The implementation calls `OutlineContent::from_path(self.tools.domain.cache(), …)` in `impl[Session<'_, D>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[dispatch]`. The test gives the tool a mock domain with its own `cache()`, so the snapshot comes from the domain's cache.\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input]` adds support for the generic source tools. It asserts that reads use the cached content, not the \"different current source\". It does not assert the outline output itself, so this is supporting evidence only.\n\n2. **Each item includes its kind.**\n   - In the paged test, every item is asserted to have `kind` equal to `fn`, or `\"\"` for the root.\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[source_outlines_present_every_top_level_and_nested_item]` asserts the exact node list. It covers `fn`, `struct`, `impl` and nested `impl[Thing]/fn[nested]`, plus the root.\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` also checks `kind == \"fn\"` for `fn[chosen]`.\n\n3. **Each item has a reference usable with `read_node`.**\n   - The paged test asserts each item's `node` equals `code.rs#fn[item_i]`, in order. It passes `items[5]` to `session.read_node`, then asserts the text is `fn item_4() {}` and that the domain recorded `code.rs#fn[item_4]`.\n   - For the generic source tools, the other tests show the selector/resource pair from the outline feeding `read_source`.\n\n4. **Follow `next` to see more items.**\n   - The paged test builds a 400-item file. It follows `next` through `get_next_page` until the last page. It asserts more than one page, non-empty chunks, `node` preserved as `code.rs#` on every page, and `items.len() == names.len() + 1`.\n   - It also asserts the order of all items and that invalid or unknown page UUIDs are rejected.\n   - Outline delivery registers no dependencies. This is checked in the paged test, in `outline_tool_rejects_excluded_and_unreadable_sources_without_domain_reads`, and in `source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads`.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that the tests would accept. The unreadable-source and rejection cases belong to `outline_source.inputs`, not this requirement.",
